{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1667","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Centroid Probabilities"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider every tree (connected undirected acyclic graph) with $$$n$$$ vertices ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$n$$$ is odd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", vertices numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$), and for each $$$2 \\le i \\le n$$$ the $$$i$$$-th vertex is adjacent to exactly one vertex with a smaller index."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$) calculate the number of trees for which the $$$i$$$-th vertex will be the centroid. The answer can be huge, output it modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A vertex is called a centroid if its removal splits the tree into subtrees with at most $$$(n-1)/2$$$ vertices each."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an odd integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\lt 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$n$$$ is odd) — the number of the vertices in the tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$n$$$ integers in a single line, the $$$i$$$-th integer is the answer for the $$$i$$$-th vertex (modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 1 0 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n10 10 4 0 0 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n276 276 132 36 0 0 0 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example $$$1$$$: there are two possible trees: with edges $$$(1-2)$$$, and $$$(1-3)$$$ — here the centroid is $$$1$$$; and with edges $$$(1-2)$$$, and $$$(2-3)$$$ — here the centroid is $$$2$$$. So the answer is $$$1, 1, 0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example $$$2$$$: there are $$$24$$$ possible trees, for example with edges $$$(1-2)$$$, $$$(2-3)$$$, $$$(3-4)$$$, and $$$(4-5)$$$. Here the centroid is $$$3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1667E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1667/problem/E"}